1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,397
SISSO doesn't hand you an answer. It hands you a pile of candidates.

2
00:00:04,777 --> 00:00:09,582
Metrics to line up by hand. And the best training fit may not be the best model.

3
00:00:09,962 --> 00:00:18,541
SISSO-Analyzer puts every candidate in one table: sortable metrics, a Pareto front, and the full formula behind every point.

4
00:00:18,921 --> 00:00:25,808
Open one: predictions, residuals, comparisons. Copy it as LaTeX, straight into your paper.

5
00:00:26,188 --> 00:00:34,963
SISSO-Sage gives your agent the evidence: shortlist models that balance prediction with physical meaning, and trace each feature to its source.

6
00:00:35,343 --> 00:00:37,074
One engine. Two readers.

7
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:40,551
From a pile of candidates, to the ones you can defend.

